# Quality gates

Run these before claiming a task is done. Failures must be fixed, not bypassed.

## Never bypass gates (binding)

**Strictly prohibited without explicit user approval:**

- File-level or block-level `eslint-disable` / `eslint-disable-next-line` for quality rules (`local/no-magic-string`, `local/max-lines-strict`, `local/complexity-strict`, `@typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any`, `@typescript-eslint/consistent-type-assertions`, `no-restricted-imports`, etc.)
- `@ts-nocheck`, `@ts-ignore`, or `@ts-expect-error` to silence gate failures
- Skipping `qualitygate:file` / `qualitygate:changed` because a file is “legacy” or “too big”
- Comments like “wave-0 extraction” to excuse disabled lint

**When a gate fails:** split the file, extract enums/helpers, fix types — do not disable the rule. If a disable is genuinely unavoidable (extremely rare), stop and ask the user first.

**Never run full-repo `tsc --noEmit` during agent work** — it is slow and OOM-prone. Use `qualitygate:file`, `qualitygate:changed`, `qualitygate:tsc` only. Full `npm run typecheck` + `npm run lint` are end-of-task only unless the user asks.

**Do not run E2E during agent work** — skip `npm run test:e2e` entirely at this stage (no smoke, no full-loop). E2E is operator/CI-only unless the user explicitly asks.

## Fast gates (during work — few seconds)

Use these while implementing. See also `todo-batch-verify.mdc` (every **5** completed todos) and `quality-backlog.mdc` (cache failures in `.local/`).

| Command | When |
|---------|------|
| `npm run qualitygate:changed` | After every **5 completed todos** or git-changed `src/**` (~5–15s) |
| `npm run qualitygate:file -- <path>` | After each single-file extract or focused edit (TSC + ESLint + **code metrics**) |
| `npm run lint:file -- <path>` | ESLint only on one file |
| `npm run qualitygate:tsc -- --changed` | Scoped TSC on git-changed files only |
| `npm run qualitygate:tsc -- --files <path>` | Scoped TSC on named file(s) |
| `npm run qualitygate:metrics` | Line count + complexity on full `src/` (also at end of `npm run typecheck`) |
| `npm run qualitygate:capture` | Scan once → cache in `.local/quality-backlog.md` (fix loop; see `quality-backlog.mdc`) |
| `npm run qualitygate:backlog` | Show cached backlog / mark items done without rescanning |

**Code metrics (warn / error):** **400 / 800** lines · complexity **15 / 25** — `.cursor/rules/code-metrics.mdc`.

**Many gate failures?** Do not re-run verify every step — `.cursor/rules/quality-backlog.mdc`.

Do **not** substitute `npm run lint`, full `npm run typecheck`, or `fabro-verify` for batch gates mid-task — too slow.

## End of task (before “done”)

```bash
npm run typecheck          # tsc --noEmit + qualitygate:metrics
npm run lint               # ESLint strict (see eslint-boundaries rule)
npm run test:unit          # Vitest
```

Optional: `npx knip` (dead code). **No E2E.**

## Module-scoped (dark-factory / commit-ready)

When `PLAN.md` names a module and you need pre-commit parity:

```bash
node scripts/fabro-verify.mjs
```

Module-scoped `tsc` + ESLint, module unit tests, then husky parity (`check-architecture`, docs, full unit, `build`). Uses `NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=6144`. Still **no E2E**.

## Full-repo reference (slow — not for batch cadence)

```bash
npm run qualitygate:tsc -- --all-slices   # all TSC slices — use sparingly
npm run check:lint         # alias for full-repo ESLint
npm run qualitygate:metrics # line/complexity only (without tsc)
```

## Baseline / ratchets

Typecheck and ESLint warnings are ratcheted — never increase the baseline count. See `docs/quality-improvement-spec.md`. `.local/` is for ad-hoc tooling (gitignored); don't add throwaway plumbing under `src/lib`.

## Order of operations (agent tasks)

1. Implement (use skills: `/refactor`, `/write-tests`, `/review`).
2. Every 5 todos: `npm run qualitygate:changed` or `npm run qualitygate:capture` → fix via backlog → continue.
3. Last todo: `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint`, `npm run test:unit`.
4. If `PLAN.md` exists and handoff is commit-ready: `node scripts/fabro-verify.mjs`.
